@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Deterministic bounded typestate evidence flow

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #495057
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F1F3F5
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "CodePropertyGraph\ntyped AST · CFG · DFG · calls" as CPG #DBE4FF
component "PropertyFsm\nstates · events · transitions\nallocations · accepting · error" as FSM #FFE8CC
component "structural validation\nclosed vocabulary · absorbing error" as VALIDATE #F1F3F5
component "typed call classification\nIdentifier / MemberAccess / target" as EVENTS #E9ECEF
component "allocation-site objects\nDFG · reference · alias worklist" as OBJECTS #FFF3BF
component "canonical function CFG\nordered may-facts (object, state)" as FACTS #D3F9D8
component "property transfer\n<latex>\delta^{\bot}(q,a)</latex>" as TRANSFER #C3FAE8
component "canonical predecessor map\nshortest stable witness" as WITNESS #FCC2D7
component "TypestateViolation\nobject · site · from · event · witness" as FINDING #FFE3E3
component "TypestateAnalysis\nterminal states · caps · issues" as REPORT #E5DBFF

CPG --> EVENTS : typed evidence only
FSM --> VALIDATE
VALIDATE --> EVENTS : valid alphabet
CPG --> OBJECTS : allocation and value flow
EVENTS --> OBJECTS : allocation events
OBJECTS --> FACTS : one identity per allocation site
CPG --> FACTS : canonical intraprocedural projection
FSM --> TRANSFER
EVENTS --> TRANSFER : ordered event occurrences
FACTS --> TRANSFER : current may-fact
TRANSFER --> FACTS : successor facts
FACTS --> WITNESS : first canonical discovery
TRANSFER --> FINDING : forbidden transition
WITNESS --> FINDING
FINDING --> REPORT
VALIDATE --> REPORT : invalid FSM issue
EVENTS --> REPORT : unresolved / ambiguous / capped
FACTS --> REPORT : terminal states and resource caps

note bottom of EVENTS
  No source-string parser exists in this analysis.
  Missing typed evidence remains explicit incompleteness.
end note

note bottom of FACTS
  Every input-sized traversal uses heap worklists and ordered maps.
  The CPG is read-only and no parallel graph is materialized.
end note

note bottom of REPORT
  Findings are advisory review evidence.
  A negative claim additionally requires is_complete().
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| represented program evidence |
|<#FFE8CC>| caller-supplied property policy |
|<#F1F3F5>| structural validation and qualification |
|<#E9ECEF>| typed event classification |
|<#FFF3BF>| abstract object/value-flow evidence |
|<#D3F9D8>| canonical CFG may-facts |
|<#C3FAE8>| property transfer |
|<#FCC2D7>| canonical witness evidence |
|<#FFE3E3>| forbidden-transition candidate |
|<#E5DBFF>| complete or explicitly partial report |
endlegend
@enduml
